# The Weaver of Stars

In the time before time, when darkness blanketed all existence, there lived a solitary weaver named Ayla in a cottage at the edge of nothingness. She possessed a loom made of moonbeam and shadow, though no moon yet existed to cast such light.

Each night, Ayla felt an ache in her heart—a longing for beauty in the endless void. So she began to weave, pulling threads from her own dreams. With each pass of her shuttle, tiny lights sparked into being, scattering across the emptiness above.

The first thread became a brilliant point she called Sun. The second formed a gentle glow she named Moon. Then came countless others—stars beyond counting, each one a crystallized fragment of hope and wonder.

